    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16117" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ergastŭlārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		ergastulum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a
			workhouse</i> or <i>house of correction</i> (late
			Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">servus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 11 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—Also: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in tenebris ergastularibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 7, 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ergastularii</span></b> , ōrum,
			m. (sc. servi), <i>overseers of a
				penitentiary</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 1, 8, 17</span></i>.</div>
